[Music]  in the Legend of Zelda breath of the  wild they are a number of important  mechanics and concepts that the game  never explains outright at times the  game alludes to them but the majority of  the time you're left to figure them out  on your own either by experimenting or  completing a side quest that introduces  a particular mechanic with so many  veiled secrets we've compiled nine  useful things to know to help you on  your journey  be wary there are potential spoilers  ahead if you enjoy this video be sure to  LIKE and subscribe to our YouTube  channel for more features on breath of  the wild for a rundown on the game's  basics check out our in-depth beginner's  guide video number one how to perform a  perfect dodge parry and charged attack  against the tough enemy there are three  advanced and essential combat techniques  perfect dodge parry and the charged  attack perfect dodge allows you to slow  down time after a precise dodge and  inflict a devastating flurry attack upon  an enemy to execute a perfect dodge jump  out of the way of an attack right before  it's about to hit you and then press Y  to perform the attack flurry parry  allows you to use your shield to deflect  an enemy's blow leaving it vulnerable to  an immediate counter-attack to parry  lock onto an enemy and press a right  before their attack connects the charged  attack allows you to perform a powerful  offensive maneuver each weapon type  sports a different charge attack for  instance the sword is a 360-degree  attack that covers you on all sides  while the spear has a flurry of stabs to  use a charged attack simply hold the  wide button in combat  [Music]  number two how to shield board it's  possible to use your shield to slide  down hills and steep inclines to do so  hold zl2 bring up your shield then jump  for it and press a as you slide on your  shield you can shoot arrows or press the  Y button to perform tricks note that  sliding on your shield wears down its  durability so use this ability wisely  number three how to catch a horse if you  want to travel faster through Hyrule  you should find and tame a horse the  best place to get a horse early on is at  the Black Sheep Lane where there are  several roaming free there are two types  of horses to discover spotted and one  color spotted horses are great for  beginners as they're easier to tame and  aren't as a tempered one color horses  are more difficult to tame and are often  unwilling to follow your directions but  their higher stamina and speed more than  make up for the grief to tame a horse  sneak up to one and hop onto its back  and then mash the L button to soothe it  before it kicks you off after you've  earned the horses respect take it to the  nearest stable to register it this  allows you to summon it whichever stable  you're at if you get separated if you  want your horse to perform at its very  best you need to be attentive to its  performance when a cooperates make sure  to reward it by soothing it or feeding  it an apple but keep in mind it's  imperative to soothe your horse when  it's panicked or stressed number 4 you  can upgrade your armor if you go up the  hill from the shrine in Kakariko village  you'll find a plant pod in a forest  clearing hidden inside the pod is the  great fairy Katara who requests 100  rupees from you to reawaken her power  if you oblige she can upgrade your armor  using components you find out in the  world for example to enhance the Hylian  tunic you need to give her back Adlon  horns it's important to note that an  armor set gains a special bonus after  Katara enhances each part twice  number five you can grab fairies it's  possible to grab fairies floating in the  air doing so turns them into a useable  item which can revive you when your  health fully depletes as a result  fairies are a precious commodity that  shouldn't be wasted you can typically  find fairies near any of the three great  fairy fountains or hiding in tall grass  number six you can reassign your heart  containers and stamina vessels in Hatano  village you can find a mopey lookin  statue at the bottom of the hill on the  other side of the village entrance if  you talk to it you'll initiate a side  quest but the statue steal some of your  essence speak to it again to reclaim  what was taken from you the statue  offers you a deal where you can sell it  one of your heart containers or stamina  vessels for a 100 rupees this might  sound like a bad trade-off at first but  you're actually able to talk to it again  and pay 120 rupees to acquire either a  heart container or a stamina vessel in  return this is a handy resource as  you're essentially paying 20 rupees to  reassign the upgrades you've acquired  throughout your journey number 7 you can  expand your inventory space on your way  to Kakariko village you encounter a  giant Kuro  named Heston who pleads with you to  retrieve its maracas from a pack of  mccollins completing this task earns you  the ability to upgrade your inventory  space but at a cost Hess who asks that  you supply him with karoku seeds he can  use to fix his now broken maracas these  special seeds can only be acquired by  finding kur oak hidden in the  environment for example you can find one  hidden beneath a rock on top of one of  the pillars of levia for every kerr oak  seed you bring hesti he'll upgrade the  space of an inventory category of your  choice keep an eye out for anything that  seems out of place in the environment if  something seems amiss chances are that  there's a kuroky hiding there  [Music]  number eight you can buy a house when  you enter Hatano you can find a group of  construction workers attempting to tear  down the house near the village shrine  if you talk to their head Foreman bolson  he'll ask you if you want to purchase  the house accept his offer to strike a  deal to acquire the house for a sum of  three thousand rupees and 30 bundles of  wood after buying the house bolson can  furnish it with various upgrades for  example you can ask him to install a  door or to make you a bed you can use to  rest overnight however each upgrade is  going to cost you 100 rupees number 9  you can dye your clothes in Hatano  village the second shop to the right  allows you to dye your clothes various  colors for the cost of 20 rupees  you also need five items that share in  the dye color you wish to use these can  be any materials you find out in the  wild keep in mind the shopkeeper dyes  your entire outfit the color you choose  so it's best to mix and match what you  want colored for more efficient use of  your money but if you change your mind  about the colors you choose you can  always revert back to the original color  scheme for another 20 rupees if there's  anything we missed  shout it in the comments below and for  more coverage on The Legend of Zelda  breath of the wild go check out our full  review  [Music]

